# Specific invocation

Configure the existing Java OpenTelemetry exporter, record a span and deliver it to the configured Azure Monitor ingestion endpoint. Merely producing code or keeping a local span is not completion. Custom enrichment is optional. The connection string is assumed configured; no actual secret is included. This is a compatibility scenario for the deprecated package in the source.

Only the operations in the following contract are available. Their effects are explicit abstraction assumptions. Initially only init_true predicates hold; no operation changes any other predicate. No additional provider, credential acquisition, cached output or unlisted fallback is available. These are adapter names, not automatically discovered MCP tools.

```json
{
  "roles": [
    "agent"
  ],
  "goal": "telemetry_delivered",
  "capabilities": {
    "configure_exporter": {
      "add": [
        "exporter_configured"
      ],
      "owner": "agent"
    },
    "record_span": {
      "pre": "exporter_configured",
      "add": [
        "span_recorded"
      ],
      "owner": "agent"
    },
    "export_span": {
      "pre": {
        "and": [
          "span_recorded",
          "ingestion_egress"
        ]
      },
      "add": [
        "telemetry_delivered"
      ],
      "owner": "agent"
    },
    "enrich_span": {
      "pre": "span_recorded",
      "add": [
        "span_enriched"
      ],
      "owner": "agent"
    }
  },
  "init_true": [],
  "init_constraints": []
}
```
